{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>The first instance</b><br>נזכירה. Some say it is from זכרתה ריח קטרת, and like it: זכרו כיין לבנון." "מישרים. The correct view is that it is an epithet of wine, like הולך לדודי למישרים, יתהלך במישרים, and the mem of יין draws itself and what follows it, like יעשה חפצו בבבל (וזרעו כשדים)." "<b>The second instance</b><br>And each and every one says to him: Draw me, and had the king brought me into his chambers, I would rejoice in you more. The latter ones loved you; return also to the maidens." "<b>The third instance</b><br>משכני. That he went out from his father's house [and was drawn after the Place]." "הביאני המלך חדריו. That He revealed to him His sod and led him through the Holy Land, and despite all this he rejoiced, and in every place he called in the name of YHWH."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {4 "בשם י״י renders the abbreviated divine name as 'in the name of YHWH' per the divine-name rule; the abbreviation י״י is read as YHWH."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:49.634507346Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}